rs/radiantgurl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/radiantgurl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-16T15:20:01Z","updated_at":"2024-11-16T15:22:17Z","body":"Why not go overboard, make a new function named `clear_task_when_complete` which will automatically handle cleaning it out of memory? Sure, you can't wait on the task anymore, and you cant check when it finishes, but neither this function can as well.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2480613032/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2480614643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99316#issuecomment-2480614643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99316","id":2480614643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T2yzz","user":{"login":"BrianBHuynh","id":51097402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDk3NDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51097402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh","html_url":"https://github.com/BrianBHuynh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-16T15:25:36Z","updated_at":"2024-11-16T15:25:36Z","body":"I was thinking it'd be nice to have a way for the developer to manually clear a task (and acknowledge that it was finished via the bool) without having to call the wait function, but yeah I think it's a good idea to implement a auto clear task function like you suggested. \r\n\r\nAtleast for me I think having something like this would be nice in general though in the case the programmer needs to acknowledge the task being completed in a way which isn't as time sensitive as using a whole wait for.\r\n\r\nI'll work on implementing a auto clear function as well though","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2480614643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482143880","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99316#issuecomment-2482143880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99316","id":2482143880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T8oKI","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T07:24:52Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T07:24:52Z","body":"I'm not quite sure this adds significant value. On the one hand, the current API is designed to mimic joining threads. Being that the case, code using the threadpool would be designed in a way that the need for something like this is avoided in the first place. On the other hand, while there may be scenarios where this may be useful, given how wary we should be of growing the engine, let alone its core, there should be a proposal, backed by a high amount of real-world demand. Other approaches would be discussed there. Also, maybe other ideas such as renaming `wait` to `join` could be scheduled for future releases, for instance.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482143880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482271522","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99316#issuecomment-2482271522","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99316","id":2482271522,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T9HUi","user":{"login":"BrianBHuynh","id":51097402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDk3NDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51097402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh","html_url":"https://github.com/BrianBHuynh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T08:33:58Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T08:33:58Z","body":"Another approach I was suggested by @RadiantUwU which may have more real world use would be the addition of a auto-clear or auto complete method, which would possibly do the same thing as this function but automatically (and without the return). Do you think that would be more useful since I've already been working on it slightly to see if I could write an implementation? I think that that may warant some extra consideration if this idea feels too frivolous of an addition\n\nThe main purpose of this addition was to make the worker threadpool more user friendly anyways, do you think that adding a bool to toggle the current wait functions instead would be a possibility? (And also the rename)\n\nI think that having a way to clear the resources without risking a wait on the main thread (and possibly a more intuitive name) may make the worker threadpool easier to use in general!\n\nPlease lmk what you think of either of those ideas since I can get working on them ASAP to see what you think! ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482271522/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2482281652","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99316#issuecomment-2482281652","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99316","id":2482281652,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6T9Jy0","user":{"login":"BrianBHuynh","id":51097402,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDk3NDAy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51097402?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh","html_url":"https://github.com/BrianBHuynh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BrianBHuynh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T08:38:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T08:38:45Z","body":"Another idea I just thought of was combining the is_completed function that was already there with the function I wrote, giving a bool (or possibly just clearing the memory on true) which would dictate if the task would be cleared from 